WEBVTT

00:03:09.972 --> 00:03:12.006
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:03:12.012 --> 00:03:13.934
Saving people, hunting things.

00:03:13.935 --> 00:03:15.257
The family business.

00:03:17.218 --> 00:03:20.356
You know the truth about
Sammy and the other children.

00:03:21.955 --> 00:03:23.594
I've known for a while.

00:03:23.608 --> 00:03:25.212
Dad, you know the demon

00:03:25.272 --> 00:03:28.063
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:03:28.212 --> 00:03:29.499
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:03:29.512 --> 00:03:31.065
No, I don't.

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:32.742
Did he say anything to you?

00:03:34.302 --> 00:03:35.231
No.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:37.963
Nothing.

00:03:38.029 --> 00:03:41.590
Max, your abilities started
6,7 months ago, right?

00:03:41.691 --> 00:03:43.955
How'd you know that? 'Cause
that's when my abilities started.

00:03:43.987 --> 00:03:44.902
You and I...

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.732
We're chosen. For what?

00:03:46.818 --> 00:03:47.874
I don't know.

00:03:47.887 --> 00:03:49.903
Everyone's capable of murder. Everyone.

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:52.025
You know, maybe that's what
the demon's doing, pushing us,

00:03:52.059 --> 00:03:53.363
Finding ways to break us.

00:03:53.369 --> 00:03:54.535
Sam, we don't know what the demon wants.

00:03:54.577 --> 00:03:56.974
We all have some kind
of ability. Ability?

00:03:57.057 --> 00:03:58.895
Psychic ability. I have visions,

00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:01.084
Premonitions. It's
different for everybody.

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:03.745
The demon said he had
plans for people like us.

00:04:03.808 --> 00:04:06.152
What kind of plans? We
don't really know for sure.

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:10.353
Don't be afraid, Scott.

00:04:10.448 --> 00:04:11.973
You can tell me anything. You know that.

00:04:13.168 --> 00:04:15.442
Whatever you say, it
won't leave this room.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:21.154
It started a little over a year ago.

00:04:22.607 --> 00:04:24.333
Migraines at first.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.724
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:04:29.237 --> 00:04:31.033
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:04:32.257 --> 00:04:33.904
I have this ability.

00:04:35.548 --> 00:04:36.974
When I touch something,

00:04:36.987 --> 00:04:39.233
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.803
How do you know?

00:04:46.057 --> 00:04:48.015
Did it to the neighbor's cat.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.794
Its insides fried up like a hamburger.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.764
You don't believe me.

00:05:02.088 --> 00:05:03.874
I believe that you believe it.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.085
Then here.

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:09.395
Want to shake on it?

00:05:21.047 --> 00:05:23.583
Why would you want to kill
the neighbor's cat, Scott?

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:24.894
I don't.

00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:28.803
He wants me to and he
doesn't want me to stop there.

00:05:28.878 --> 00:05:29.923
Who?

00:05:31.827 --> 00:05:33.213
The yellow-Eyed man.

00:05:33.678 --> 00:05:35.582
He comes to me in my dreams.

00:05:36.157 --> 00:05:38.732
He tells me to do things, awful things

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.243
But I tell him no.

00:05:42.278 --> 00:05:43.892
"No, I don't want to!"

00:05:44.838 --> 00:05:47.254
What else does the
yellow-Eyed man tell you?

00:05:52.459 --> 00:05:54.185
He has plans for me.

00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:55.835
What kind of plans?

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.714
And you've just had
some kind of mushroom

00:06:01.717 --> 00:06:06.293
And your mind is moving low

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.012
Go ask Alice

00:06:10.377 --> 00:06:13.175
I think she'll know

00:06:15.829 --> 00:06:19.363
When logic and proportion

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:20.354
Hello?

00:06:20.408 --> 00:06:24.303
Have fallen softly dead

00:06:24.319 --> 00:06:28.994
And the white knight
is talking backwards

00:06:29.058 --> 00:06:33.274
And the red queen's, "off with her head"

00:06:34.048 --> 00:06:36.442
Remember

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:40.482
What the dormouse said

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.394
Feed your head

00:07:02.157 --> 00:07:03.763
Before dad died, he...

00:07:04.268 --> 00:07:05.854
He told me something.

00:07:07.808 --> 00:07:09.354
Something about you.

00:07:11.188 --> 00:07:12.435
What?

00:07:16.189 --> 00:07:17.853
Dean, what did he tell you?

00:07:18.918 --> 00:07:19.875
He said that he...

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.962
Wanted me to watch out for you...

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.504
Take care of you.

00:07:26.458 --> 00:07:28.325
He told you that a million times.

00:07:28.378 --> 00:07:29.692
Well, this time was different.

00:07:31.197 --> 00:07:32.492
He said that I had to...

00:07:34.028 --> 00:07:35.242
Save you.

00:07:36.677 --> 00:07:38.023
Save me from what?

00:07:38.117 --> 00:07:39.995
He just said that I had to save you

00:07:39.997 --> 00:07:41.244
And nothing else mattered

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.164
And that if I couldn't, I'd...

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.874
You'd what, Dean?

00:07:48.309 --> 00:07:49.725
I'd have to kill you.

00:07:54.489 --> 00:07:57.004
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sammy.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.734
Kill me?

00:08:01.508 --> 00:08:03.522
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:08:03.587 --> 00:08:04.383
I don't know.

00:08:04.459 --> 00:08:06.605
He must have had some kinda
reason for saying it, right?

00:08:07.318 --> 00:08:08.743
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.774
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.955
What else did he say,
Dean? That's it, I swear.

00:08:13.988 --> 00:08:16.144
How could you not have told
me this? Because it was dad,

00:08:16.179 --> 00:08:17.913
And he begged me not to. Who cares!

00:08:17.948 --> 00:08:20.272
Take some responsibility
for yourself, Dean!

00:08:20.527 --> 00:08:22.453
You had no right to keep this from me!

00:08:22.558 --> 00:08:23.814
You  think I wanted this?

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.334
Huh?

00:08:25.459 --> 00:08:27.812
I wish to god he'd
never opened his mouth.

00:08:28.479 --> 00:08:31.623
Then I wouldn't have to walk around
with this screaming in my head all day!

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:40.612
We each got to figure
out what's going on,

00:08:40.618 --> 00:08:42.304
Then, what the hell all this means.

00:08:44.967 --> 00:08:46.035
We do?

00:08:46.618 --> 00:08:49.132
I've been thinking about this.
I think we should just lay low,

00:08:49.179 --> 00:08:51.322
You  know. At least for a while.

00:08:51.368 --> 00:08:52.715
It would be safer.

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.463
That way, I could make sure...

00:08:55.558 --> 00:08:56.554
What?

00:08:57.548 --> 00:08:59.224
That I don't turn evil?

00:08:59.247 --> 00:09:01.872
That I don't turn into
some kind of killer?

00:09:01.878 --> 00:09:03.584
I never said that.
Jeez, you're not careful,

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.302
You will have to waste me one day, Dean.

00:09:05.409 --> 00:09:06.544
I never said that!

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:10.685
Damn it, Sam, this whole thing
is spinning out of control.

00:09:11.208 --> 00:09:13.873
All right? You're immune
to some weirdo demon virus

00:09:14.979 --> 00:09:16.994
And I don't even know
what the hell anymore.

00:09:20.688 --> 00:09:23.603
And you're pissed at me, and I
get it. That's fine. I deserve it.

00:09:25.487 --> 00:09:28.445
But we lay low until we
figure out our next move, okay?

00:09:28.528 --> 00:09:29.732
Forget it.

00:09:31.698 --> 00:09:33.684
Sam, please, man.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:35.475
Hey, please.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.623
Just give me some time.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.752
Give me some time to think, okay?

00:09:40.788 --> 00:09:43.484
I'm begging you here. Please, please...

00:12:10.089 --> 00:12:10.973
Honey?

00:12:13.049 --> 00:12:14.293
Are you okay?

00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:16.064
Oh, I just had another nightmare.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.572
It's fine. It's nothing.

00:12:17.679 --> 00:12:19.173
Just go back to sleep.

00:12:19.798 --> 00:12:20.974
Sure?

00:12:22.028 --> 00:12:23.834
Yeah. Okay.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:44.964
Sam.

00:12:45.187 --> 00:12:46.355
Hey, Ellen.

00:12:48.898 --> 00:12:51.015
You don't seem that surprised to see me.

00:12:51.049 --> 00:12:52.575
Your brother's been
calling, worry to say,

00:12:52.578 --> 00:12:54.065
Looking for you. Yeah.

00:12:54.497 --> 00:12:55.753
I figured he might.

00:12:55.789 --> 00:12:57.563
What's going on between you two?

00:12:59.977 --> 00:13:01.072
So, um...

00:13:02.142 --> 00:13:03.451
How's Jo?

00:13:05.904 --> 00:13:07.513
Well, I don't really know.

00:13:07.559 --> 00:13:09.980
What do you mean? I
haven't seen her in weeks.

00:13:10.061 --> 00:13:11.893
She sends a postcard now and again.

00:13:11.919 --> 00:13:13.183
Well, what happened?

00:13:13.199 --> 00:13:15.914
Well, after she worked
that job with you boys

00:13:15.989 --> 00:13:17.795
She decided she wanted
to keep on hunting.

00:13:18.398 --> 00:13:20.142
I said, "not under my roof,"

00:13:20.148 --> 00:13:22.305
And she said "fine".

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.752
So I'm probably the last person
you want to see right now.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.124
Oh, don't get me wrong.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.185
I wish I could blame
the hell out of you boys.

00:13:35.918 --> 00:13:37.173
It would be easier.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.162
The truth is, it's not your fault.

00:13:40.589 --> 00:13:41.882
Sam,

00:13:42.468 --> 00:13:43.964
None of it is.

00:13:46.937 --> 00:13:48.432
I want you to know that

00:13:49.049 --> 00:13:51.475
I forgave your daddy a long time ago...

00:13:52.527 --> 00:13:54.342
For what happened to my Bill.

00:13:56.009 --> 00:13:58.493
I just don't think he
ever forgave himself.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.154
What did happen?

00:14:05.037 --> 00:14:08.105
Um, so, why did you come here, sweetie?

00:14:09.979 --> 00:14:11.305
I need help.

00:14:11.458 --> 00:14:13.124
So, what am I looking for, Sam?

00:14:13.167 --> 00:14:15.072
Other people, other...

00:14:15.518 --> 00:14:17.245
Psychics like me.

00:14:17.349 --> 00:14:20.653
As many as possible and I
need a nationwide search.

00:14:20.708 --> 00:14:21.834
But

00:14:21.838 --> 00:14:24.143
I thought there was no
way to track them all down.

00:14:24.238 --> 00:14:26.573
Not all of them had
nursery fires like you did.

00:14:27.057 --> 00:14:27.974
Well...

00:14:27.977 --> 00:14:29.955
No, but some had to.

00:14:29.999 --> 00:14:31.043
Start there.

00:14:35.267 --> 00:14:36.105
Done...

00:14:36.108 --> 00:14:37.354
And done.

00:14:37.459 --> 00:14:39.133
That was fast. Well,

00:14:39.169 --> 00:14:41.053
Apparently, that's my job.

00:14:41.138 --> 00:14:43.363
Make the monkey dance. Key boarding.

00:14:43.387 --> 00:14:45.135
Just tell us what you got, Ash.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:48.882
Four folks fit the profile nationwide.

00:14:48.939 --> 00:14:51.812
Born in '83, mother
died in a nursery fire,

00:14:51.848 --> 00:14:53.864
The whole shebang. Four? That's it?

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.874
Sam Winchester from Lawrence, Kansas.

00:14:56.938 --> 00:14:58.614
Max Miller from Saginaw, Michigan,

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.102
Andrew Gallagher from Guthrie, Oklahoma

00:15:01.999 --> 00:15:03.062
And

00:15:03.077 --> 00:15:04.925
Another name,

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.144
Scott Carey.

00:15:08.207 --> 00:15:09.493
What? You got an address?

00:15:09.519 --> 00:15:10.633
Kind of.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:16.123
The arbor hills cemetery
in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:15:16.187 --> 00:15:18.653
Plot 486. So he's dead?

00:15:18.749 --> 00:15:21.555
Killed about a month ago. Killed how?

00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:22.822
Stabbed.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.555
Parking lot.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:26.954
Fuzz don't have much.

00:15:27.437 --> 00:15:28.905
No suspects.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:32.942
All right.

00:15:33.239 --> 00:15:34.605
Thank you.

00:15:39.469 --> 00:15:41.464
Where are you going? Indiana.

00:15:41.549 --> 00:15:42.523
Sam,

00:15:43.389 --> 00:15:45.495
I got to call Dean. I've got
to let him know where you are.

00:15:45.568 --> 00:15:47.894
Ellen, I'm trying to find answers

00:15:47.899 --> 00:15:49.514
About who I am

00:15:50.019 --> 00:15:53.345
And my brother means well, but
he can't protect me from that.

00:15:55.159 --> 00:15:56.363
Please.

00:16:01.869 --> 00:16:03.882
You said you went to
high school with Scott?

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.384
Uh, yes, sir, I did.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.585
I just heard about what
happened. I'm so sorry.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.374
Scotty was a good boy.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.383
He changed a lot since you knew him.

00:16:14.429 --> 00:16:15.965
What do you mean?

00:16:16.369 --> 00:16:19.775
It started about a year
ago with these headaches.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.835
Then he got depressed, paranoid.

00:16:23.308 --> 00:16:25.372
Nightmares. Nightmares?

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.355
Did he ever talk to you about
his nightmares, what he saw?

00:16:31.458 --> 00:16:32.482
No, no,

00:16:33.019 --> 00:16:34.455
He  closed up on me.

00:16:34.469 --> 00:16:36.825
I  tried to get him
help, but nothing took.

00:16:37.557 --> 00:16:38.685
He'd just...

00:16:39.488 --> 00:16:41.664
Lock himself in his room for days.

00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:44.992
You think maybe I could see his room?

00:18:04.789 --> 00:18:06.384
Who are you? Please...

00:18:07.007 --> 00:18:08.373
You're in danger.

00:18:09.507 --> 00:18:12.213
Okay, look, I know how all this sounds,

00:18:12.218 --> 00:18:14.952
But I am not insane,
and I'm not on drugs.

00:18:15.059 --> 00:18:16.615
Okay, I am normal,

00:18:16.647 --> 00:18:19.314
And this is way, way off the map for me.

00:18:19.339 --> 00:18:20.464
All right, all right, just...

00:18:21.048 --> 00:18:23.054
Just calm down, okay?

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:25.662
What's your name? Ava.

00:18:25.709 --> 00:18:27.075
Ava? Ava Wilson.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.522
Ava, I'm Sam Winchester, all right?

00:18:29.598 --> 00:18:33.182
Now, you were telling me
about these dreams of yours?

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.113
Oh, yeah, uh, okay.

00:18:35.119 --> 00:18:38.675
About a year ago, I started having
these like headaches, and just...

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:41.813
Nightmares, I guess. And I
really didn't think much of it

00:18:41.917 --> 00:18:46.123
Until I had this one dream where I saw
this guy get stabbed in a parking lot.

00:18:47.458 --> 00:18:48.894
When was this?

00:18:48.938 --> 00:18:51.612
Uh, about a month ago. But anyway,

00:18:51.657 --> 00:18:53.432
A couple of days later...

00:18:54.999 --> 00:18:56.523
I found this.

00:19:00.107 --> 00:19:02.353
I saw this guy die

00:19:02.358 --> 00:19:04.722
Days before it happened.

00:19:04.748 --> 00:19:07.765
I don't know why. I don't
know. It's just for some reason,

00:19:08.459 --> 00:19:11.145
My dreams are coming true,

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:12.353
And

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.052
Last night,

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.835
I had another one.

00:19:16.517 --> 00:19:17.624
Okay.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:19.133
About you.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:23.092
I saw you die.

00:19:27.189 --> 00:19:28.484
How did you find me?

00:19:29.759 --> 00:19:32.423
You had motel stationery,
and I googled the motel,

00:19:32.509 --> 00:19:35.625
And it was real, and so I
just thought that I should

00:19:35.629 --> 00:19:37.072
Warn you.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.274
I don't believe this.

00:19:41.749 --> 00:19:43.303
Of course you don't.

00:19:43.378 --> 00:19:45.424
You think I'm a total nutjob.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.254
Wait! No, no, no.

00:19:47.338 --> 00:19:49.424
I mean, you must be one of us.

00:19:50.159 --> 00:19:52.735
Sorry, one of... One of who?

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.643
One of the psychics, like me.

00:19:56.157 --> 00:19:57.225
Look, Ava, I have visions too, all
right? So... so we're connected.

00:20:03.739 --> 00:20:06.324
Okay, so... you're nuts.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.962
That's great. No,
okay, okay. Okay, look.

00:20:08.997 --> 00:20:12.003
Did your mother happen
to die in a house fire?

00:20:12.097 --> 00:20:14.465
No, my mother lives in Palm Beach.

00:20:14.527 --> 00:20:16.473
So you don't fit the pattern either.

00:20:23.488 --> 00:20:24.484
Hello?

00:20:24.529 --> 00:20:25.473
It's Ellen.

00:20:25.507 --> 00:20:26.905
Hey, have you heard from Sam?

00:20:27.009 --> 00:20:27.933
I have.

00:20:27.938 --> 00:20:31.295
But he made me promise not
to tell you where he is.

00:20:31.319 --> 00:20:32.753
Come on, Ellen, please.

00:20:32.859 --> 00:20:34.795
Something bad could be
going on here, and I swore

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.155
I'd look after that kid.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.282
Dean, let's say you can't
protect your loved ones forever.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:42.255
Well, I say screw that.

00:20:42.298 --> 00:20:43.742
What else is family for?

00:20:45.459 --> 00:20:47.305
He's in Lafayette, Indiana.

00:20:48.139 --> 00:20:49.094
Thanks.

00:20:50.527 --> 00:20:52.225
Why can't you just leave town,

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.955
Please, before you blow up?

00:20:55.027 --> 00:20:56.204
No, I can't.

00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:58.974
Oh, god. Why not?

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:01.404
Because there's something
going on here, Ava,

00:21:01.908 --> 00:21:03.313
With you, with me.

00:21:03.479 --> 00:21:05.534
I mean, there are
others like us out there

00:21:05.619 --> 00:21:07.975
And we're all a part of something,

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.202
And I've got to figure out what.

00:21:10.288 --> 00:21:12.212
Okay, you know what?

00:21:12.729 --> 00:21:14.452
Screw you, buddy. Okay?

00:21:14.488 --> 00:21:17.282
'Cause I'm a secretary from Peoria
and I'm not part of anything.

00:21:17.938 --> 00:21:18.813
Do you see this?

00:21:18.847 --> 00:21:21.072
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:21:21.158 --> 00:21:23.065
I am supposed to be at
home addressing invitations

00:21:23.107 --> 00:21:25.525
Which I am way behind on, by the way.

00:21:25.579 --> 00:21:29.063
But instead, I drove out
here to save your weirdo ass.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:32.804
But if you just want to
stay here and die, fine.

00:21:33.037 --> 00:21:34.104
Me?

00:21:34.158 --> 00:21:36.154
I'm due back on planet earth.

00:21:36.239 --> 00:21:38.094
Don't you wanna know
why this is happening?

00:21:39.807 --> 00:21:42.495
I mean, don't these visions
scare the hell out of you?

00:21:44.049 --> 00:21:46.375
'Cause if you walk out
that door right now,

00:21:47.689 --> 00:21:49.593
You might never know the truth.

00:21:53.477 --> 00:21:55.015
I need your help.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:57.185
So, Miss Wilson, you're new in town?

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:58.913
That's right.

00:21:58.989 --> 00:22:01.434
And what made you decide
to seek out therapy?

00:22:02.959 --> 00:22:04.613
I have no idea.

00:22:05.009 --> 00:22:05.962
No?

00:22:06.048 --> 00:22:09.184
No, I mean, I'm feeling really, super...

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:12.433
Anxious right now.

00:22:12.519 --> 00:22:14.494
Okay, anything else?

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.515
Holy crap! What?!

00:22:24.047 --> 00:22:26.622
I just remembered, when I was a kid,

00:22:26.657 --> 00:22:29.403
I swallowed like eight things of pop
rocks, and then drank a whole can of coke.

00:22:29.488 --> 00:22:32.605
You don't think that that counts
as a suicide attempt, do you?

00:22:42.550 --> 00:22:43.965
You okay?

00:22:45.499 --> 00:22:46.702
Am I okay?

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:47.635
Yeah.

00:22:47.689 --> 00:22:51.343
I just helped you steal some dead
guy's confidential psych files.

00:22:51.547 --> 00:22:53.064
I'm awesome!

00:22:54.517 --> 00:22:56.262
It started a little over a year ago.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:58.664
Migraines at first.

00:22:59.809 --> 00:23:02.844
Then I found I could do stuff.

00:23:02.919 --> 00:23:04.272
What do you mean, "do stuff"?

00:23:04.297 --> 00:23:05.682
I have this ability.

00:23:07.479 --> 00:23:09.074
When I touch something,

00:23:09.077 --> 00:23:11.302
I can electrocute it if I want.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.914
Oh, thank god you're okay.

00:23:40.977 --> 00:23:42.842
Oh, you're better than okay.

00:23:42.867 --> 00:23:45.382
Sam, you sly dog.

00:23:47.187 --> 00:23:49.332
What else does the yellow-Eyed man say?

00:23:49.858 --> 00:23:52.562
He has plans for me.

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:57.425
He says there's a war coming,

00:23:57.967 --> 00:24:00.072
And people like me...

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.012
We're gonna be the soldiers.

00:24:02.469 --> 00:24:04.733
Everything is about to change.

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:08.015
He's not talking about us, right?

00:24:08.720 --> 00:24:10.443
Yeah, I think he is.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:18.322
Well... but how can we turn into that?

00:24:21.489 --> 00:24:22.494
I don't...

00:24:23.780 --> 00:24:25.052
Get down! Oh my god!

00:24:25.877 --> 00:24:27.405
Oh, my god, what's happening?

00:24:41.247 --> 00:24:42.102
Gordon!

00:24:49.157 --> 00:24:50.635
You do that to my brother,

00:24:50.638 --> 00:24:52.393
I'll kill you! Dean, wait!

00:25:11.527 --> 00:25:13.752
Wait, I don't understand.

00:25:13.860 --> 00:25:16.263
Shouldn't we be talking to the cops?

00:25:17.017 --> 00:25:19.324
Trust me, they wouldn't do us much good.

00:25:26.538 --> 00:25:29.353
These are 223 caliber, subsonic rounds.

00:25:29.439 --> 00:25:31.833
The guy must have put a
suppressor on the rifle.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:35.873
Dude, who are you?!

00:25:36.470 --> 00:25:38.742
Oh, I just, uh

00:25:39.259 --> 00:25:41.502
I just watch a lot of "T.J.Hooker".

00:25:46.517 --> 00:25:47.614
Who you calling?

00:25:47.649 --> 00:25:48.564
My brother.

00:25:48.657 --> 00:25:50.522
I think we definitely need help.

00:25:51.528 --> 00:25:52.512
Hello?

00:25:52.527 --> 00:25:54.602
Dean. Sam, I've been looking for you.

00:25:55.008 --> 00:25:57.195
Yeah, look, I'm in Indiana.

00:25:57.227 --> 00:25:59.354
Lafayette. I know.

00:25:59.457 --> 00:26:00.404
You do?

00:26:01.150 --> 00:26:02.682
Yeah, I talked to Ellen.

00:26:02.727 --> 00:26:04.485
I just got here myself.

00:26:04.819 --> 00:26:06.575
It's a real funky town.

00:26:06.997 --> 00:26:08.942
You ditched me, Sammy.

00:26:09.037 --> 00:26:12.332
Yeah, I'm sorry. Look, right now,

00:26:12.419 --> 00:26:14.265
There's someone after me. What? Who?

00:26:14.327 --> 00:26:16.404
I don't know. That's
what we need to find out.

00:26:17.130 --> 00:26:18.434
Where are you?

00:26:18.450 --> 00:26:22.344
I'm staying at 5637 Monroe
street. Why don't you meet me here?

00:26:22.399 --> 00:26:23.414
Yeah,  sure.

00:26:27.398 --> 00:26:28.825
Now, was that so hard?

00:26:29.489 --> 00:26:30.804
Bite me.

00:26:32.347 --> 00:26:33.483
What is it?

00:26:33.497 --> 00:26:34.903
My brother's in trouble.

00:26:35.057 --> 00:26:35.803
What?

00:26:36.469 --> 00:26:38.155
He gave me a code word.

00:26:38.559 --> 00:26:40.152
Someone's got a gun on him.

00:26:40.780 --> 00:26:42.774
Code word? Yeah.

00:26:42.799 --> 00:26:44.144
"Funky town"

00:26:45.847 --> 00:26:47.852
Well, he thought of it.

00:26:47.889 --> 00:26:48.825
It's kind of a

00:26:48.837 --> 00:26:50.012
Long story.

00:26:50.557 --> 00:26:51.522
Come on.

00:26:53.178 --> 00:26:54.115
Gordy,

00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:57.185
I know me and Sam ain't exactly
your favorite people, but,

00:26:57.528 --> 00:26:59.524
Don't you think this
is a little extreme?

00:27:00.020 --> 00:27:02.044
Oh, you think this is revenge?

00:27:02.867 --> 00:27:05.563
We did leave you tied up in
your own mess for three days.

00:27:05.668 --> 00:27:07.062
Which was awesome.

00:27:07.817 --> 00:27:09.802
Sorry, I shouldn't laugh. Yeah,

00:27:10.767 --> 00:27:13.425
I was definitely planning on
whupping your ass for that.

00:27:13.998 --> 00:27:16.753
That's not what this
is. This isn't personal.

00:27:18.018 --> 00:27:20.774
I'm not a killer, Dean.

00:27:21.217 --> 00:27:22.474
I'm a hunter.

00:27:23.458 --> 00:27:25.595
And your brother is fair game.

00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:31.052
I don't think I should leave.

00:27:31.110 --> 00:27:33.142
I want you out of harm's way, Ava.

00:27:33.637 --> 00:27:34.975
What about you?

00:27:35.069 --> 00:27:36.783
Harm's way doesn't really bother me.

00:27:36.798 --> 00:27:37.702
No, but,

00:27:37.710 --> 00:27:39.822
You are walking right into my vision.

00:27:39.838 --> 00:27:41.375
I mean, this is how you die!

00:27:41.407 --> 00:27:42.823
It doesn't matter.

00:27:44.367 --> 00:27:45.835
It's my brother.

00:27:46.168 --> 00:27:47.722
Maybe I can help.

00:27:47.778 --> 00:27:49.422
You've done all you can. Just...

00:27:49.950 --> 00:27:51.633
Just go back to your fianc.

00:27:52.929 --> 00:27:54.012
Are you sure?

00:27:55.039 --> 00:27:56.693
Yes, I'm sure.

00:27:56.987 --> 00:27:58.353
Go home, Ava.

00:27:58.420 --> 00:27:59.814
You'll be safe there.

00:28:04.467 --> 00:28:05.533
Well, just...

00:28:07.547 --> 00:28:09.095
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:28:09.107 --> 00:28:12.253
When you get your brother, just let
me know that everything's all right.

00:28:13.017 --> 00:28:14.285
I promise.

00:28:15.588 --> 00:28:18.702
See, I was doing an
exorcism down in Louisiana.

00:28:19.127 --> 00:28:21.843
A teenage girl. It seemed routine.

00:28:21.928 --> 00:28:23.564
Some low-Level demon.

00:28:23.627 --> 00:28:26.003
But between all the jabbering
and the head-Spinning,

00:28:26.048 --> 00:28:29.314
The damn thing muttered
something about a coming war.

00:28:29.349 --> 00:28:31.745
I don't think it meant to.
It just kind of slipped out.

00:28:31.779 --> 00:28:32.983
But it was too late.

00:28:33.029 --> 00:28:34.742
It piqued my interest.

00:28:34.790 --> 00:28:38.272
And you can really make a demon
talk when you got the right tools.

00:28:38.338 --> 00:28:40.595
What happened to the
girl it was possessing?

00:28:40.649 --> 00:28:42.105
She didn't make it.

00:28:43.669 --> 00:28:45.535
Well, you're a son of a bitch.

00:28:51.478 --> 00:28:53.503
That's my mama you're talking about.

00:28:55.050 --> 00:28:56.164
Anyway,

00:28:57.327 --> 00:29:01.363
This demon tells me they have
soldiers to fight in this coming war.

00:29:01.379 --> 00:29:04.012
Humans fighting on hell's
side. You believe that?

00:29:04.418 --> 00:29:08.424
I mean, they're psychics, so they're
not exactly pure humans. But still,

00:29:08.457 --> 00:29:12.452
What kind of worthless scumbag you got
to be to turn against your own race?

00:29:14.427 --> 00:29:16.363
But you know the
biggest kick in the ass?

00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:19.115
This demon said I knew one of them

00:29:19.959 --> 00:29:22.655
Our very own Sammy Winchester.

00:29:25.999 --> 00:29:27.035
Well, this is...

00:29:27.117 --> 00:29:29.205
This is a whole new level of moronic,

00:29:29.298 --> 00:29:31.054
Even for you. Yeah?

00:29:32.180 --> 00:29:33.522
Come on, Dean.

00:29:33.527 --> 00:29:34.875
I know

00:29:34.879 --> 00:29:36.945
About Sam's visions.

00:29:38.439 --> 00:29:40.443
I know everything. Really?

00:29:40.838 --> 00:29:42.712
Because a demon told you?

00:29:42.877 --> 00:29:45.283
Yeah, and it wasn't lying. Hey, Dean,

00:29:45.757 --> 00:29:49.035
I'm not some reckless yahoo,
okay? I did my homework.

00:29:49.137 --> 00:29:50.863
I made damn sure it was true.

00:29:51.528 --> 00:29:54.393
Look, you got your
Roadhouse connections.

00:29:54.827 --> 00:29:56.113
I got mine.

00:29:56.520 --> 00:29:59.064
It's how I found Sammy
in the first place.

00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:10.502
About a month ago, I found another
one of these freaks here in town.

00:30:10.540 --> 00:30:13.094
He could deep-Fry a person
just by touching them.

00:30:13.127 --> 00:30:14.563
Yeah, did he kill anyone?

00:30:14.657 --> 00:30:17.242
Besides mr. Tinkles, the cat, no.

00:30:17.308 --> 00:30:19.015
But he was working up to it.

00:30:19.977 --> 00:30:21.813
They're all gonna be killers, Dean.

00:30:21.839 --> 00:30:23.374
We got to take them all out,

00:30:23.380 --> 00:30:25.502
And that means Sammy too.

00:30:30.457 --> 00:30:32.773
You think Sam's stupid enough
to walk through that front door?

00:30:32.847 --> 00:30:34.554
No, I don't.

00:30:34.928 --> 00:30:37.622
Especially since I'm sure
you found a way to warn him.

00:30:40.020 --> 00:30:42.173
You really think I'm that stupid?

00:30:48.049 --> 00:30:49.184
No,

00:30:50.079 --> 00:30:52.605
Sammy's gonna scope the place first,

00:30:53.459 --> 00:30:55.613
See me covering the front door.

00:30:57.010 --> 00:30:59.054
So he's gonna take the back.

00:31:00.048 --> 00:31:02.472
And when he does,
he'll hit the tripwire.

00:31:04.058 --> 00:31:05.274
Then...

00:31:10.179 --> 00:31:11.404
Boom.

00:31:12.608 --> 00:31:15.303
Sam's not gonna fall
for a frickin' tripwire.

00:31:16.490 --> 00:31:17.883
Maybe you're right.

00:31:20.990 --> 00:31:22.914
That's why I'll have a second one.

00:31:28.749 --> 00:31:29.933
Hey, look,

00:31:30.978 --> 00:31:32.314
I'm sorry.

00:31:33.089 --> 00:31:35.644
I wish I didn't have
to do this. I really do.

00:31:36.768 --> 00:31:38.394
But for what it's worth,

00:31:39.517 --> 00:31:41.155
It will be quick.

00:32:13.479 --> 00:32:14.625
Come on, man.

00:32:15.349 --> 00:32:17.885
I know Sam, okay? Better than anyone.

00:32:18.358 --> 00:32:20.282
He's got more of a
conscience than I do. I mean,

00:32:20.320 --> 00:32:22.282
The guy feels guilty surfing
the internet for porn.

00:32:22.317 --> 00:32:23.303
Maybe you're right,

00:32:23.969 --> 00:32:25.974
But one day, he's gonna be a monster.

00:32:26.008 --> 00:32:26.774
How?

00:32:27.278 --> 00:32:29.523
Huh? How's a guy like
Sam become a monster?

00:32:29.548 --> 00:32:32.272
It beats me, but he will.
No, you don't know that!

00:32:33.909 --> 00:32:35.492
I'm surprised at you, Dean.

00:32:36.080 --> 00:32:37.652
Getting all emotional.

00:32:38.668 --> 00:32:41.594
I had heard you were more
of a professional than this.

00:32:44.510 --> 00:32:45.434
Look,

00:32:45.447 --> 00:32:49.523
Let's say you're cruising
around in that car of yours.

00:32:49.557 --> 00:32:50.753
And uh,

00:32:50.959 --> 00:32:54.483
You have little Hitler
riding shotgun, right?

00:32:55.008 --> 00:32:56.452
Back when he was just some

00:32:56.458 --> 00:32:58.912
Goofy, crappy artist.

00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:02.904
But you knew what he was
gonna turn into someday.

00:33:03.810 --> 00:33:05.305
You'd take him out.

00:33:05.687 --> 00:33:07.485
No questions, am I right?

00:33:07.529 --> 00:33:09.275
That's not Sam. Yes, it is.

00:33:10.058 --> 00:33:11.853
You just can't see it yet.

00:33:14.460 --> 00:33:17.014
Dean, it's his destiny.

00:33:20.037 --> 00:33:21.113
Look,

00:33:21.117 --> 00:33:23.035
I'm sympathetic.

00:33:23.490 --> 00:33:25.342
He's your brother. You love the guy.

00:33:26.027 --> 00:33:28.473
This has got to hurt like hell for you.

00:33:34.018 --> 00:33:35.704
But here's the thing.

00:33:38.280 --> 00:33:39.784
It would have wrecked him,

00:33:40.899 --> 00:33:42.105
But your dad

00:33:43.530 --> 00:33:45.313
If it really came right down to it,

00:33:45.357 --> 00:33:48.013
He would have had the stones
to do the right thing here.

00:33:49.048 --> 00:33:50.652
So, you're telling me

00:33:51.508 --> 00:33:53.462
You're not the man he is?

00:35:11.168 --> 00:35:12.513
You hear him?

00:35:26.220 --> 00:35:27.685
Here he comes.

00:35:34.167 --> 00:35:35.315
Hold on.

00:35:35.729 --> 00:35:37.165
Not yet.

00:35:37.969 --> 00:35:39.653
Let's wait and see.

00:36:03.107 --> 00:36:04.434
Sorry, Dean.

00:36:29.040 --> 00:36:30.435
Drop the gun.

00:36:31.739 --> 00:36:34.002
You shouldn't take your
shoes off around here.

00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:36.914
You might get tetanus. Put it down now!

00:36:44.359 --> 00:36:45.973
You wouldn't shoot me, would you, Sammy?

00:36:46.747 --> 00:36:49.663
'Cause your brother, he thinks
you're some kind of saint.

00:36:50.068 --> 00:36:51.264
Yeah.

00:36:51.358 --> 00:36:52.562
Well, I wouldn't be so sure.

00:36:53.488 --> 00:36:55.252
See, that's what I said.

00:37:19.699 --> 00:37:22.622
You're no better than the
filthy things you hunt.

00:37:40.529 --> 00:37:41.634
Do it.

00:37:42.460 --> 00:37:43.674
Do it!

00:37:44.159 --> 00:37:46.744
Show your brother the
killer you really are, Sammy.

00:37:55.100 --> 00:37:56.574
It's Sam.

00:38:28.508 --> 00:38:31.424
Son of a bitch... Dean, no.

00:38:31.868 --> 00:38:34.324
I let him live once. I'm not
making the same mistake twice.

00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:35.412
Trust me.

00:38:36.040 --> 00:38:37.854
Gordon's taken care of.

00:38:39.468 --> 00:38:40.482
Come on.

00:39:03.258 --> 00:39:04.884
You call this taken care of?

00:39:09.539 --> 00:39:10.745
What the hell are we doing?

00:39:10.807 --> 00:39:12.425
Just trust me on this. All right?

00:39:20.319 --> 00:39:22.653
Drop your weapons!
Get down on your knees!

00:39:22.689 --> 00:39:24.025
Do it now!

00:39:34.508 --> 00:39:36.044
Put your hands on your head.

00:39:37.120 --> 00:39:38.612
Easy now.

00:39:57.488 --> 00:39:59.193
Anonymous tip.

00:39:59.957 --> 00:40:02.575
You're a fine, upstanding citizen, Sam.

00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:16.684
Gordon Walker was hunting Sam?

00:40:16.698 --> 00:40:18.055
And he almost killed us both 'cause

00:40:18.087 --> 00:40:20.065
Somebody over there can't
keep their frickin' mouth shut.

00:40:20.470 --> 00:40:22.414
And you honestly think that it was me?

00:40:22.910 --> 00:40:23.804
Or Ash or Jo?

00:40:23.808 --> 00:40:24.694
No way.

00:40:24.730 --> 00:40:26.254
Who else knows about Sam, huh?

00:40:27.457 --> 00:40:29.274
Well, you must have
been talking to somebody.

00:40:29.327 --> 00:40:31.413
You can say a lot of things about us

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:32.744
But we aren't disloyal,

00:40:32.749 --> 00:40:34.103
And we're not stupid.

00:40:34.139 --> 00:40:35.815
We haven't breathed a word of this.

00:40:35.879 --> 00:40:37.895
Gordon said he had
Roadhouse connections, Ellen.

00:40:37.908 --> 00:40:40.695
And this Roadhouse is
full of other hunters.

00:40:42.268 --> 00:40:45.122
They're all smart.
They're good trackers,

00:40:45.168 --> 00:40:48.083
Each of them with their own
patterns and connections.

00:40:48.139 --> 00:40:50.463
Hell, I could name 12 of them right now

00:40:50.470 --> 00:40:52.554
That are capable of
putting this together.

00:40:54.788 --> 00:40:57.125
I am sorry about what happened, Dean,

00:40:57.987 --> 00:40:59.973
But I can't control these people

00:40:59.979 --> 00:41:02.134
Or what they choose to believe.

00:41:08.447 --> 00:41:10.615
Hey, Ava, it's Sam... again.

00:41:11.499 --> 00:41:12.632
Call me when you get this.

00:41:12.738 --> 00:41:14.904
Just want to make
sure you got home okay.

00:41:15.437 --> 00:41:16.995
All right, bye.

00:41:17.009 --> 00:41:18.622
Everything all right?

00:41:19.407 --> 00:41:21.495
Yeah, I hope so.

00:41:21.528 --> 00:41:24.664
Well, Gordon should be reaching for the
soap for the next few years, at least.

00:41:24.749 --> 00:41:25.655
Yeah,

00:41:26.019 --> 00:41:28.523
If they pin Scott
Carey's murder on him...

00:41:29.010 --> 00:41:30.745
And if he doesn't bust out.

00:41:33.337 --> 00:41:35.652
Dude, you ever take
off like that again...

00:41:37.530 --> 00:41:38.662
What?

00:41:38.848 --> 00:41:40.302
You'd kill me?

00:41:41.457 --> 00:41:43.095
That's so not funny.

00:41:44.139 --> 00:41:45.112
All right.

00:41:45.819 --> 00:41:48.085
All right. So, where to next then?

00:41:48.117 --> 00:41:49.153
One word,

00:41:49.639 --> 00:41:51.572
Amsterdam. Dean...

00:41:51.618 --> 00:41:54.264
Come on, man, I hear the coffee
shops don't even serve coffee.

00:41:54.368 --> 00:41:56.704
I'm not gonna just ditch
the job. Screw the job.

00:41:57.250 --> 00:41:59.392
Screw it, man. I'm
sick of the job anyway.

00:41:59.449 --> 00:42:00.505
We don't get paid.

00:42:00.539 --> 00:42:01.643
We don't get thanked.

00:42:01.729 --> 00:42:03.214
The only thing we get is bad luck.

00:42:03.898 --> 00:42:05.662
Well, come on dude, you're a hunter.

00:42:05.768 --> 00:42:08.034
I mean, it's what you were meant to
do. I wasn't meant to do anything.

00:42:08.070 --> 00:42:09.842
I don't believe in that destiny crap.

00:42:09.920 --> 00:42:11.993
You mean you don't
believe in my destiny.

00:42:13.270 --> 00:42:14.442
Whatever.

00:42:15.617 --> 00:42:17.433
Look, Dean, I've tried running before.

00:42:17.867 --> 00:42:20.433
I mean, I ran all the way to
California, and look what happened.

00:42:21.200 --> 00:42:22.763
You can't run from this,

00:42:22.770 --> 00:42:24.444
And you can't protect me.

00:42:26.980 --> 00:42:28.304
I can try.

00:42:30.977 --> 00:42:32.382
Thanks for that.

00:42:36.829 --> 00:42:38.905
Look, Dean, I'm gonna keep hunting.

00:42:39.828 --> 00:42:41.114
I mean, whatever's coming,

00:42:41.738 --> 00:42:44.862
I'm taking it head on so if
you really want to watch my back

00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:47.272
Then I guess you're gonna
have to stick around.

00:42:47.998 --> 00:42:49.844
Bitch. Jerk.

00:42:56.488 --> 00:42:57.952
You calling that Ava girl again?

00:42:57.980 --> 00:42:59.562
You sweet on her or something?

00:43:00.909 --> 00:43:02.623
She's engaged, Dean.

00:43:02.668 --> 00:43:03.704
So?

00:43:04.289 --> 00:43:05.502
What's the point in saving the world,

00:43:05.508 --> 00:43:07.584
If you can't get a little
nookie once in a while, huh?

00:43:10.588 --> 00:43:11.825
What?

00:43:12.827 --> 00:43:14.205
Just a feeling.

00:43:16.467 --> 00:43:18.683
How far is it to Peoria?

00:43:28.550 --> 00:43:29.424
Hello?

00:43:32.538 --> 00:43:34.102
Is anybody home?

00:43:46.037 --> 00:43:47.344
My god...

00:44:04.207 --> 00:44:05.235
Hey.

00:44:08.647 --> 00:44:10.074
Sulfur.

00:44:13.639 --> 00:44:15.143
The demon's been here.

00:44:36.529 --> 00:44:37.924
Ava...



00:03:09.952 --> 00:03:11.452
